{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Dinner for Four", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Too Much to Eat", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Looking to the Stars > Famous People", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 3, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Identify and describe personal and regional eating habits and cooking in  a range of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Writes short texts about presenting plans for a future activity at work using correct spelling, grammar, cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to the communicative", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Writing a Recipe (Quantifiers)", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "To write a recipe you need to follow these steps:  <ul><li>First, write the list of ingredients.</li> <li>Second, include the amount of ingredients you need.</li> <li>Third, specify time of preparation.</li> <li>Fourth, add number of servings.</li> <li>Fifth, write the instructions to prepare your dish in steps and complete sentences.</li> <li>Sixth, add a last recommendation.</li></ul>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Basic sponge cake</span><br>Preparation time: 45 minutes.<br> Servings: for 8 people<br>  Ingredients:<br> 8 ounces self-raising flour<br> 8 ounces butter 8 ounces caster sugar<br> 4 eggs<br> 1 teaspoon baking powder<br><br>  Preparation:<br> 1. Preheat the oven to 180 degrees.<br> 2. Measure all the ingredients into a large bowl.<br> 3. Mix all of the ingredients using an electric whisk.<br> 4. Pour the mixture into 2 non-stick 7 inch (18 cm) tins.<br> 5. Place them in the oven till golden brown 15-25 minutes.<br> 6. Cool on a wire rack before serving.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing What is Necessary", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the following to express what is necessary: <ul>  \t<li>You had better \u2026</li> \t<li>You have got to \u2026</li> \t<li>I'm going to have to \u2026 </li> \t<li>You need to ...</li>  </ul>   \t\t\t", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Bob</span>: You've got to come to our downtown office!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class =\"strong\">Waiter</span>: Sir, I'm going to have to ask you to turn your phone off.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "crockpot", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a heated container to slow cook meals", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I've never had a meal made with a crockpot. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in the kitchen.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rosemary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a green herb used in cooking", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can smell the rosemary and garlic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sponge cake", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a light cake made with flour and egg whites", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  How does sponge cake for dessert sound?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "punnet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small box to hold soft fruit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Where is the punnet of strawberries?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sifted", "type": "name"}, {"content": "put flour or sugar through a sifter or sieve to remove lumps or big particles", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Add the sifted flour to the mixture.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le03ob08aud05", "type"